sentences.l:
And the Argives gave way from the ships, indeed, and by necessity
from the foremost ones, but on the spot beside the huts they stayed,
all together, and did not scatter up through the army;

And many fine swords, dark-bound, hilted,
some indeed from hands fell to the ground, and others from the shoulders
of men fighting;

And whichever of the Trojans came on against the hollow ships
with blazing fire, as a favour to Hector, who had urged them on,
him Ajax would wound, awaiting him with his long spear;
